<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-18938] lu object free eats so much time</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18938</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;While worked on unlink and zfs scalability problems &lt;br/&gt;
I found object free eats so much time of unlink, it caused an extra cpu load in the ARC cache flush thread.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;16) &amp;lt;...&amp;gt;-2682981 | .... 7.184 us   |     mdd_trans_stop [mdd]();
 16) &amp;lt;...&amp;gt;-2682981 | ....+ 62.367 us  |   } /* mdd_unlink [mdd] */
 16) &amp;lt;...&amp;gt;-2682981 | .... 0.030 us   |   mutex_unlock();
 16) &amp;lt;...&amp;gt;-2682981 | ....+ 43.762 us  |     lu_object_free.isra.36 [obdclass]();
 16) &amp;lt;...&amp;gt;-2682981 | ....+ 46.206 us  |   } /* lu_object_put [obdclass] */
 16) &amp;lt;...&amp;gt;-2682981 | ....! 154.269 us | } /* mdt_reint_unlink [mdt] */
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In short evaluation unlink perf increased by 10%-20% by moving object free into separate thread. ZFS have benefits from this change also.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
